        <time datetime="2026-08-24">August 24, 2026</time>
        <h1>Acclaimed as your next Pakenham Ward Councillor</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="post-body">
        <p>
          Well folks, it is official: I am acclaimed as your next Pakenham
          Ward councillor ahead of this fall's municipal election! This means
          that I've been selected as the councillor and will not be
          campaigning over the coming months, and no ballots will need to be
          cast for me since no one else had decided to run in the same ward.
          As a first-time candidate, I feel fortunate to have garnered enough
          trust of those around me to represent everyone's interests, while
          also recognising that I also haven't earned everybody's support by
          default.
        </p>

        <p>
          For the first time in nearly four decades, Denny Ferguson, a
          mainstay of municipal politics in Pakenham, will be enjoying a
          well-deserved break. I'd like to thank him and his family for
          putting so much of their time towards our neighbours, and I am
          honoured to take those reins.
        </p>

        <p>
          Putting my name in for this councillor position came from a desire
          to achieve even more of what brings me so much joy: fostering
          culture in our community, flexing my pragmatic, innovation-loving
          problem solving skills, and stepping up when I see places where I
          can use the experience I've got.
        </p>

        <p>
          I've got a laundry list of notes on my phone for things that I want
          to share, ask or do with everyone over the next while, all of which
          I'm expecting will get us better acquainted ahead of the middle of
          November when I will be sworn in. While these things trickle out
          over the next couple of months, I wanted to share at least some
          core information here and now so you can tell your neighbours who
          are also wondering who this "Travis Jordan" lad is.
        </p>

        <h2>Here's what you might care to know right now</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>
            I'm the only Tavis Joron out there, and it's easy to mispronounce
            or misspell my name. I won't ever judge you if that happens, but
            if you want to get it right from the get-go, I like to break it
            down as Tavis rhymes with Travis but there's no "r", and Joron
            rhymes with moron but with a J instead of an M 😅
          </li>
          <li>
            I grew up in Almonte and spent my life there before moving first
            to Ottawa for half a decade, then back to Almonte for a year, and
            I've been in Pakenham with my wife for 5 years.
          </li>
          <li>
            I'll be 34 years old next month, have no kids, but have 2 cats
            and a puppy.
          </li>
          <li>
            I live right in the village on Jessie street backing onto the
            arena, with the chaotic-looking vegetable gardens in my side yard
            and a Seedling Library sign that I've had set up since the
            spring. You can't miss it on your way to the park, beach or
            baseball diamond.
          </li>
          <li>
            I work remotely full-time in Total Rewards (Compensation) for
            Canadian Nuclear Labs. My career spans a dozen years working in
            Human Resources or HR-adjacent roles in high tech, and on the
            day-to-day I am mostly found in Excel spreadsheets, developing
            information management tools using a programming language
            (Python), or meeting with over a dozen union reps as we
            collaborate as a committee as part of the federal Pay Equity
            Act's requirements.
          </li>
          <li>
            I've got zero experience as a politician, have no agenda
            whatsoever coming into the role, and have a reputation of not
            picking sides in debates and heated conversations.
          </li>
          <li>
            I place large value on sticking to logical, factual and
            constructive conversations. I love measuring data, having
            supporting evidence, and receiving feedback. My opinion can and
            will change on subjects as information is presented.
          </li>
          <li>
            Outside of work I am typically found walking my dog Goose,
            gardening, playing volleyball, organising community events,
            chatting with neighbours, or out in the wilderness
            foraging/hunting/fishing/hiking/photographing.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Huge thanks to everyone who has supported me so far, and I am very
          much honoured and excited to join our council and make our towns
          even better places to live.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          Pictured: me and Goose, our 9 month old medium bernedoodle, on one
          of our many walks to the park to play.
        </blockquote>
